+# obj.eval) are not. Fixed text is fixed code however it's written: any string literal (raw, triple-quoted, prefixed,
+# an f-string or template literal with no placeholder), adjacent literals, or literals joined only by +. Anything
+# else is flagged, including an f-string or template literal with a placeholder.
+#
+# A finding needs both: the argument has some part that isn't a string literal (metavariable-pattern), and its
+# source text isn't a run of literals joined by + (metavariable-regex). Either alone excludes fixed text.
 rules:
   - id: factory.js-eval-of-built-string
     languages: [javascript, typescript]
     severity: ERROR
     message: >-
-      $FN evaluates a string built at run time as code: whatever ends up in it runs unreviewed. Call the code
